{"ts":"2026-11-26T03:32:01Z","sha":"9e830bfa94fe69c9c3a49882540a5196ed5452e5","round":1,"kind":"finding","file":"_acceptance/upgrade-design-assembly-0-69-0/rang/lint-scope.mjs","title":"lint-scope measure (AC-7) passes when ESLint lints none of the three probe files","severity":"medium","source":"bugs","inContract":false,"acRef":"","plain":"If a later config change silently stopped checking the tool folder and the probe files, the acceptance check would still report green. Today's product is not affected; only the check's ability to warn is weaker.","can_cu":"No user-facing harm now since the current setup is correct; it only weakens an internal safety net for a future mistake, and can be fixed cheaply later if that mistake ever becomes likely.","proposal":"known-limits","khongBacBo":true,"unverified":false,"unclassified":false}
{"ts":"2026-11-26T03:32:01Z","sha":"9e830bfa94fe69c9c3a49882540a5196ed5452e5","round":1,"kind":"finding","file":"_acceptance/upgrade-design-assembly-0-69-0/rang/two-way.mjs","title":"Shape 5 (claims a class sweep but has only point cases): tool-tree has nine red conditions, and the two-way pairing shows only five of them failing","severity":"medium","source":"measurement","inContract":false,"acRef":"","plain":"Four ways the tool version record could drift from the plugin's templates were never shown to be caught by the check. Users see no effect now, but a future drift of that kind might go unnoticed.","can_cu":"The current state is correct and verified green; the gap only affects how well the check catches future drift, and it can be added later without any user impact.","proposal":"known-limits","khongBacBo":true,"unverified":false,"unclassified":false}
